          },
          "create_time": 1791397240,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "For Project Alpha we call the PayFlow API for every charge. When it gets slow under high traffic, should we use exponential backoff or a circuit breaker?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "m1": {
        "id": "m1",
        "parent": "m0",
        "children": [
          "m2"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m1",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1791397280,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Use both, for different jobs. Exponential backoff with jitter and a retry limit handles transient failures like timeouts and 503s. A circuit breaker stops hammering a provider that is clearly down. For payments, the critical piece is an idempotency key on every charge so a retry after a timeout cannot double-charge a customer."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {
            "model_slug": "gpt-5"
          }
        }
      },
      "m2": {
        "id": "m2",
        "parent": "m1",
        "children": [
          "m3"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m2",
          "author": {
            "role": "user"
          },
          "create_time": 1791397320,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "What timeout should we use if our p99 checkout budget is 800 ms?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "m3": {
        "id": "m3",
        "parent": "m2",
        "children": [],
        "message": {
          "id": "m3",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1791397360,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Keep the per-attempt client timeout well under the budget. Many teams use an 800 ms ceiling for the whole call and move retries off the request path with asynchronous processing on a queue, so checkout returns immediately and a worker retries in the background."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {
            "model_slug": "gpt-5"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "current_node": "m3",
    "conversation_id": "conv-43-4"
  },
